WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:05.730
A lot of uncertainty still surrounds the accidental
shooting and death of cinematographer Halyna

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:08.850
Hutchins on the set of the Alec Baldwin film
"Rust."

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:13.950
It's a very important topic in Hollywood right
now, due to both the tragic death of Hutchins

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:18.320
and the debate over how effective safety measures
are on film sets.

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:23.150
Either way, there's been a lot of reports
on what exactly happened on the set of "Rust,"

00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:27.659
from the news that prop guns may have been
used for target practice to an official affidavit

00:00:27.659 --> 00:00:32.000
that reveals members of the camera crew walked
off set prior to the shooting.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:37.110
The tragedy has also brought into focus the
larger issue of penny-pinching producers cutting

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:43.120
corners on productions by hiring inexperienced
- and often non-union - staff in critical

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:44.120
roles.

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:49.170
When prop masters and armorers don't have
the proper training or experience, the stage

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:53.540
is pretty well set for a terrible accident
like this one.

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:58.289
To be clear, this is a fast-moving story,
and the details are still coming into focus

00:00:58.289 --> 00:01:04.040
as a variety of authorities continue the investigations
and more staffers close to the project talk

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:05.040
to the press.

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:12.230
We don't yet know exactly which - if any - dangerous
corners were cut on the set of "Rust," but

00:01:12.230 --> 00:01:17.860
the few details that have come to light suggest
an accident like this one might have been

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:19.080
foreseeable.

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:23.880
A new exclusive report by The Wrap claims
that the armorer, who is the person in charge

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:29.370
of prop weapons on a film set, for "Rust,"
Hannah Gutierrez-Reed, was at the center of

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:34.570
controversy over gun safety on her last project,
the Nicolas Cage film "The Old Way."

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:40.570
If the report is to be believed, there's a
lot of information here to suggest that Gutierrez-Reed

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:44.160
may have been far too inexperienced for the
job.

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:49.200
According to The Wrap, which cited "The Old
Way" key grip Stu Brumbaugh, armorer Hannah

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:53.860
Gutierrez-Reed irresponsibly fired weapons
near the cast and crew and even drew the ire

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:56.210
of star Nicolas Cage at one point.

00:01:56.210 --> 00:02:01.730
The actor allegedly yelled at Gutierrez-Reed,
saying that she blew out his eardrums.

00:02:01.730 --> 00:02:06.300
Soon after that, Brumbaugh apparently demanded
that she be fired from "The Old Way" for being

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:09.130
too inexperienced and unsafe at her job.

00:02:09.130 --> 00:02:10.130
He recalled,

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:13.420
"I told the AD, 'She needs to be let go.

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:16.190
After the second round I was pissed off.

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:17.830
We were moving too fast.

00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:18.920
She's a rookie."

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:23.350
It's also important to note, however, that
The Wrap reached out to an unnamed producer

00:02:23.350 --> 00:02:28.860
to confirm elements of Brumbaugh's testimony,
and this producer refuted the information

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:29.860
saying,

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:32.800
"I have no such recollection of this event
on our set.

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:35.050
I asked my partners the same.

00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:39.380
The details on some of these accounts specifically
when it pertains to 'The Old Way' have been

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:41.069
blown out of proportion."

00:02:41.069 --> 00:02:48.630
So, once again, while this would be very big
news if proven true, there's not enough quite

00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:50.470
yet to say either way.

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:54.830
There's a chance that might change, however,
as the investigation into the shooting on

00:02:54.830 --> 00:02:56.410
"Rust" continues.

00:02:56.410 --> 00:03:02.510
One thing's for certain, no one in Hollywood
wants to be anywhere near this incident - even

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:08.459
vicariously - and it doesn't take much of
a leap to imagine an unnamed producer might

00:03:08.459 --> 00:03:13.100
want to stamp out any suggestion that they
didn't perform their due diligence before

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:16.440
hiring an armorer to handle prop weapons on
set.

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:21.460
It may be some time before we have clear picture
of everything that transpired on the "Rust"

00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:27.640
set that fateful day, but anecdotal evidence
- much of it well reported by credible outlets

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:33.390
- is beginning to mount that at least some
liberties were taken with best practices for

00:03:33.390 --> 00:03:40.090
handling prop firearms on set, and that poorly
trained or inexperienced staff may have been

00:03:40.090 --> 00:03:42.610
hired to help the movie's bottom line.

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:48.440
It's the latest tragic data point in an unfortunate
industry trend of producers from the financial

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:54.750
services sector applying too much of a market-capitalist
mentality to the process of filmmaking.

00:03:54.750 --> 00:04:00.950
Movies have always been a business, and businesses
have to turn a profit, but profits don't always

00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:06.510
have to be maximized to the detriment of working
conditions and good conscience.

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:12.000
"Rookie," non-union production staffers are
less expensive, but the cost of realizing

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:18.129
those financial savings is an elevated risk
to the cast, crew, and - ultimately - the

00:04:18.129 --> 00:04:19.959
production itself.

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:26.139
The incident on "Rust" is just about the worst
imaginable repercussion of this kind of corner-cutting.

00:04:26.139 --> 00:04:30.360
If Brumbaugh's account of what transpired
with Hannah Gutierrez-Reed on the set of "The

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:35.909
Old Way" proves credible, it will be one more
piece of evidence that may stack up to massive

00:04:35.909 --> 00:04:41.520
civil liability for "Rust" producers - and
potentially even criminal charges.

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:47.539
None of that can ever bring Halyna Hutchins
back, but severe legal consequences in this

00:04:47.539 --> 00:04:53.650
case might at least make penny-pinching producers
think twice about cutting corners when it

00:04:53.650 --> 00:04:55.479
comes to safety on set.

